message.content:
Set up pg_cron scheduled jobs on Supabase project `jaumyfyeueayibbxunxc` to call 4 edge functions on schedule.

Use the Supabase MCP tools (apply_migration / execute_sql).

STEP 1 — Enable extensions (run via execute_sql):
```sql
create extension if not exists pg_cron;
create extension if not exists pg_net;
```

STEP 2 — Check if extensions enabled successfully. If pg_cron or pg_net fail to enable, report that immediately and stop.

STEP 3 — Apply this migration (use apply_migration with name "mia_behavioral_cron_schedules"). The 4 edge functions were deployed with verify_jwt=false so they are publicly callable (no auth header needed). Function base URL is https://jaumyfyeueayibbxunxc.supabase.co/functions/v1/

```sql
-- Idempotent: unschedule existing jobs with same names first
do $$
declare j record;
begin
  for j in select jobname from cron.job where jobname in (
    'mia-morning-digest','mia-anomaly-watcher','mia-pattern-analyzer','mia-distillation'
  ) loop
    perform cron.unschedule(j.jobname);
  end loop;
end $$;

-- Morning digest: 07:30 BRT = 10:30 UTC daily
select cron.schedule('mia-morning-digest', '30 10 * * *', $job$
  select net.http_post(
    url := 'https://jaumyfyeueayibbxunxc.supabase.co/functions/v1/mia-morning-digest',
    headers := '{"Content-Type":"application/json"}'::jsonb,
    body := '{}'::jsonb,
    timeout_milliseconds := 30000
  );
$job$);

-- Anomaly watcher: every 15 minutes
select cron.schedule('mia-anomaly-watcher', '*/15 * * * *', $job$
  select net.http_post(
    url := 'https://jaumyfyeueayibbxunxc.supabase.co/functions/v1/mia-anomaly-watcher',
    headers := '{"Content-Type":"application/json"}'::jsonb,
    body := '{}'::jsonb,
    timeout_milliseconds := 30000
  );
$job$);

-- Pattern analyzer: 23:00 BRT = 02:00 UTC daily
select cron.schedule('mia-pattern-analyzer', '0 2 * * *', $job$
  select net.http_post(
    url := 'https://jaumyfyeueayibbxunxc.supabase.co/functions/v1/mia-pattern-analyzer',
    headers := '{"Content-Type":"application/json"}'::jsonb,
    body := '{}'::jsonb,
    timeout_milliseconds := 60000
  );
$job$);

-- Distillation: Sunday 02:00 BRT = Sunday 05:00 UTC weekly
select cron.schedule('mia-distillation', '0 5 * * 0', $job$
  select net.http_post(
    url := 'https://jaumyfyeueayibbxunxc.supabase.co/functions/v1/mia-distillation',
    headers := '{"Content-Type":"application/json"}'::jsonb,
    body := '{}'::jsonb,
    timeout_milliseconds := 120000
  );
$job$);
```

STEP 4 — Verify by running:
```sql
select jobid, jobname, schedule, active from cron.job where jobname like 'mia-%' order by jobname;
```

Report back: which extensions were enabled, all 4 cron jobs with their schedule and active status, and any errors. Be precise and factual.
